+\subsection{Research Track: Planck-Scale Route Audit and Preregistered Route-A Target}
+\label{subsec:rt_planck_routes_v3_preregistered_audit}
+
+\paragraph{Status.}
+\textbf{[RESEARCH-TRACK] [TRIAL] [NOT DERIVED] [FITTED].}
+This subsection records a negative-control audit of four Planck-scale route
+candidates.  The candidates are not independent confirmations.  They are four
+algebraic representations of one trial seed relation once the Compton--core and
+horn-density closures are used.  Consequently, the shared residual is not
+evidence for convergent derivations; it is one residual written in four
+variables.  The only retained scientific value is a sharpened target for a
+future Route-A vacuum-tangle derivation.
+
+\paragraph{Single seed relation.}
+The common seed candidate is
+\begin{align}
+    G_{\star}
+    &=
+    \frac{\pi^3}{16}\,
+    \frac{\rho_{\!f}\,\vchar^{9}\,r_c^4}{M_e^2 c^7},
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_seed_G}
+    \\
+    &=
+    \frac{\pi^3}{2^{17}}\,
+    \alpha_{\rm SST}^{13}\,
+    \frac{\rho_{\!f}\,\hbar^4}{M_e^6c^2},
+    \qquad
+    \alpha_{\rm SST}\equiv\frac{2\vchar}{c},
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_seed_alpha_form}
+\end{align}
+where the second form uses the Compton--core closure
+\begin{align}
+    \hbar\simeq\frac{M_ec^2r_c}{\vchar}.
+\end{align}
+With the current numerical constants,
+\begin{align}
+    G_{\star}
+    &=6.6361514\times10^{-11}\,
+    \mathrm{m^3\,kg^{-1}\,s^{-2}},
+    &
+    \frac{G_{\star}}{G_N}&=0.99428425,
+    \\
+    t_{p,\star}
+    &=\sqrt{\frac{\hbar G_{\star}}{c^5}}
+    =5.3758171\times10^{-44}\,\mathrm{s},
+    &
+    \frac{t_{p,\star}}{t_p}&=0.99713808.
+\end{align}
+This numerical proximity is a target only, not a derivation of
+\(G\), \(L_p\), or \(t_p\).
+
+\paragraph{Four route representations of one seed.}
+The line-density representation is
+\begin{align}
+    \left(\sigma_{\rm pierce}\Lambda_L\right)_A
+    =
+    \frac{16}{\pi^2}\,
+    \frac{\rho_{\rm core}}{\rho_{\!f}}
+    \left(\frac{c}{\vchar}\right)^6
+    \frac{1}{r_c^2} .
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_route_A}
+\end{align}
+The induced-mode representation is
+\begin{align}
+    N_B
+    =
+    2r_c^2\left(\sigma_{\rm pierce}\Lambda_L\right)_A
+    =
+    \frac{32}{\pi^2}\,
+    \frac{\rho_{\rm core}}{\rho_{\!f}}
+    \left(\frac{c}{\vchar}\right)^6 .
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_route_B}
+\end{align}
+The pressure-susceptibility representation is
+\begin{align}
+    G_C
+    =
+    \frac{\pi^2}{32}\,
+    \frac{\rho_{\!f}}{\rho_{\rm core}}
+    \left(\frac{\vchar}{c}\right)^5
+    \frac{\vchar^2r_c}{M_e} .
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_route_C}
+\end{align}
+The maximum-tension representation is its reciprocal force-bound form,
+\begin{align}
+    F_D=\frac{c^4}{4G_C}.
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_route_D}
+\end{align}
+Equivalently, using the horn-density closure to eliminate \(G_C\),
+\begin{align}
+    F_D
+    =
+    \frac{16}{\pi^2}\,
+    F_{\rm swirl}^{\max}
+    \frac{\rho_{\rm core}}{\rho_{\!f}}
+    \left(\frac{c}{\vchar}\right)^7,
+\end{align}
+up to the rounding used in the tabulated \(F_{\rm swirl}^{\max}\).
+
+\paragraph{Equivalence lemma.}
+Under the closure relations
+\begin{align}
+    \hbar\simeq\frac{M_ec^2r_c}{\vchar},
+    \qquad
+    \rho_{\rm core}\simeq
+    \frac{M_ec^2}{2\pi\vchar^2r_c^3},
+\end{align}
+one obtains
+\begin{align}
+    N_B
+    &=2r_c^2\left(\sigma_{\rm pierce}\Lambda_L\right)_A,
+    \\
+    2\left(\sigma_{\rm pierce}\Lambda_L\right)_A
+    \frac{\hbar G_C}{c^3}
+    &\simeq1,
+    \\
+    F_D&=\frac{c^4}{4G_C},
+    \\
+    G_C&\simeq G_{\star}.
+\end{align}
+The small difference between the unreduced \(G_C\) value and the fully reduced
+\(G_{\star}\) value is a constant-synchronization artifact caused by finite
+precision in \(\rho_{\rm core}\) and the Compton--core \(\hbar\) closure.  It is
+not a separate physical residual.
+
+\paragraph{Look-elsewhere disclosure.}
+The negative-control scan used
+\begin{align}
+    G
+    =
+    G_0
+    \left(\frac{\rho_{\!f}}{\rho_{\rm core}}\right)^k
+    \left(\frac{\vchar}{c}\right)^n
+    \pi^p2^m,
+    \qquad
+    G_0=\frac{\vchar^2r_c}{M_e},
+\end{align}
+with
+\begin{align}
+    k\in[-3,3],\quad
+    n\in[-20,20],\quad
+    p\in[-8,8],\quad
+    m\in[-12,12].
+\end{align}
+This is a grid of \(121{,}975\) candidates.  In that grid, \(31\) candidates
+fall within \(5\%\) of \(G_N\), and \(5\) candidates fall within \(0.575\%\).
+A better numerical hit exists in the same grid with
+\((k,n,p,m)=(0,15,-6,7)\), i.e. without the density ratio.  Therefore the
+sub-percent match of Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_planck_v3_seed_G} has no evidentiary
+force unless the exponent structure and kernel are derived independently before
+comparison.
+
+\paragraph{Degeneracy disclosure.}
+Exact closure of Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_planck_v3_seed_G} to \(G_N\) would require
+\begin{align}
+    \rho_{\!f}^{\rm exact}
+    =7.04024\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}},
+\end{align}
+whereas the current canonical value is rounded as
+\(\rho_{\!f}=7.0\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}\).  Moreover,
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_planck_v3_seed_alpha_form} scales as
+\begin{align}
+    \frac{\partial\ln G_{\star}}{\partial\ln\alpha_{\rm SST}}=13,
+\end{align}
+so a fractional shift of order \(4.4\times10^{-4}\) in the effective
+\(\vchar/c\) calibration absorbs the residual.  The residual is therefore
+degenerate among \(\rho_{\!f}\), \(\alpha_{\rm SST}\), and the fitted
+angular/kernel factor.
+
+\paragraph{Preregistered Route-A target.}
+The useful non-circular target is
+\begin{align}
+    \sigma_{\rm pierce}\Lambda_L
+    \stackrel{?}{=}
+    \frac{1}{2L_p^2}
+    =1.9140\times10^{69}\,\mathrm{m^{-2}}.
+    \label{eq:rt_planck_v3_route_A_target}
+\end{align}
+This target may be used only for final comparison.  A valid future Route-A
+model must derive \(\Lambda_L\) and \(\sigma_{\rm pierce}\) from SST
+vacuum-tangle statistics without using \(G\), \(L_p\), \(t_p\), or
+\(F_{\rm gr}^{\max}\) as inputs.  The model must predeclare its line-density
+definition, orientation distribution, entropy per piercing, and kernel factors
+before numerical comparison.  Additional coefficient scans are negative controls
+only and do not count as evidence.
